      "id": "kf1da3j",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Forces Controlling Winds"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Wind velocity and direction are determined by the interaction of Pressure Gradient Force, Coriolis Force, and Friction.",
        "Planetary winds (Trade Winds, Westerlies, and Polar Easterlies) blow persistently across global pressure belts throughout the year.",
        "Monsoons are periodic seasonal winds caused by differential heating and cooling of landmasses and oceans.",
        "Local winds are micro-climatic winds categorized into warm winds (e.g., Chinook, Loo, Fohn) and cold winds (e.g., Mistral, Bora).",
        "Jet streams are narrow bands of high-velocity westerly winds in the upper troposphere that influence global surface weather patterns."
      ],
      "id": "h3t3enk"
    },
